# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Rachna's per-project convenience folder. Holds nothing load-bearing: the
# real state (store, shims, disks, snapshots) lives in
# ~/.local/share/rachna/<project-id>/, outside the workspace mount, because the
# guest can write anything inside the project folder.
# See design-docs/08-POLICY-AND-STORE.md §4.
/.rachna

# Devenv
.devenv*
devenv.local.nix
devenv.local.yaml

# direnv
.direnv

# pre-commit
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# cargo-mutants working output
/mutants.out
/mutants.out.old

# Internal working notes: kept on disk, never committed.
#
# "Don't add it in git but still keep them" — and the first attempt at that
# DESTROYED them. `git-filter-repo` stripped them from all 185 commits and
# rewrote every ref including the backup branch made beforehand, after which
# the objects were garbage-collected. They were rebuilt from this session's
# transcript, which had every heredoc that wrote them.
#
# So they are ignored rather than removed: present in the working tree,
# absent from history. A master copy also lives in ~/rachna-design-docs.
/design-docs/
/AGENTS.md
/idea.md
